[rest omitted]

	I put in my $0.02 and second the idea.

>Oh yeah, while I'm at it, how about having some way of telling whether a
>corpse is rotted or not? (Short of sacrificing or eating it, naturally...)

	Yes, I would like to know also.  I once had two stone giant corpses
on the ground (I know, I know, I shouldn't have killed two at once), and the
top one was rotting, which I discovered when I tried to eat it.  However, it
would not let me choose to eat the other one.  I always got the message,
"There are two stone giant corpses here.  Eat one? [yn]"  Maybe they both
were rotten, but it would be nice to have a choice.  Maybe a command to
smell something...

	#sniff
	In what direction? >
	You sniff the stone giant corpse--more--
	It smells like rotting carrion.

Or, for some humor...(or identification when blind...[ ] quantity omitted when
blind):

	#sniff
	In what direction?  6
	[You sniff in the direction of the troll--more--]
	You reel at the malodorous (sp?) scent.

	#sniff
	In what direction?  4
	[You sniff in the direction of the nymph--more--]
	You smell Chanel No. 5.

	#sniff
	In what direction? 8
	[You sniff in the direction of the red dragon--more--]
	You smell sulfurous whisps of smoke.

OK, enough.

